  "verbalization": "Gomisin C is consistently linked to Jurkat through a series of molecular targets, with the endothelial lipase serving as a common intermediary. This lipase is targeted by multiple isoforms of the compound, including (4aR,8aS)-4a,7,7-trimethyl-3,4,5,6,8,8a-hexahydro-1H-naphthalen-2-one and 1-[(2S,3S)-2-(3-Hydroxyprop-1-En-2-Yl)-3-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-Trihydroxy-6-(Hydroxymethyl)Oxan-2-Yl]Oxy-2,3-Dihydro-1-Benzofuran-5-Yl]Ethanone. These compounds all share a common mechanism of action, targeting the same enzyme and ultimately leading to a relationship with Jurkat. The evidence suggests that Gomisin C exerts its biological effect through a shared pathway involving endothelial lipase, which is then targeted by multiple related compounds, ultimately leading to a relationship with Jurkat. The consistency across different molecular isoforms supports a unified mechanism, highlighting the importance of endothelial lipase in mediating the interaction between Gomisin C and Jurkat.",
